[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5359643011","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122481#issuecomment-5359643011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122481","id":5359643011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABP3Wpgw","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-20T17:49:58Z","updated_at":"2026-08-20T17:49:58Z","body":"The code in question:\n\n```\nVariant ClassDB::class_get_default_property_value(const StringName &p_class, const StringName &p_property, bool *r_valid) {\n    if (!default_values_cached.has(p_class)) {\n        if (!default_values.has(p_class)) {\n            default_values[p_class] = HashMap<StringName, Variant>();\n        }\n```\n\nSo it seems pretty easy for `default_values_cached` or `default_values` getting stomped on. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5359643011/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5703113685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122481#issuecomment-5703113685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122481","id":5703113685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU-6b1Q","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T19:12:38Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T19:12:38Z","body":"I think this was solved for 4.8 by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123546. If not, please let us know and we'll reopen.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5703113685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5707211004","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122481#issuecomment-5707211004","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122481","id":5707211004,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVC0g_A","user":{"login":"migueldeicaza","id":36863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza","html_url":"https://github.com/migueldeicaza","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-17T01:50:48Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T01:50:48Z","body":"The fix in the bug is incomplete, see my comments.\n\nI suggest that when using AI generated PRs, that users use the /code-review tool, as it would help reduce that noise.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5707211004/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5724750544","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122481#issuecomment-5724750544","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122481","id":5724750544,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVTjC0A","user":{"login":"exaltedo2","id":173569997,"node_id":"U_kgDOClh3zQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173569997?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2","html_url":"https://github.com/exaltedo2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/exaltedo2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-18T03:32:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-18T03:32:00Z","body":"#123594 does not make ClassDB thread-safe. Aside from this PR, I investigated how ClassDB could be made thread-safe. Here are the issues I found:\n\n`get_placeholder_extension()` — It writes to the `placeholder_extensions` map at line 723, but the scope of the read lock there ends at line 720, leaving the write operation completely unprotected by a lock. Furthermore, it continues to use the `ClassInfo*` pointer—which references the `classes` map—after releasing the read lock. It also executes on worker threads via `_instantiate_internal()` at line 616.\nAs far as I can tell, `set_current_api()`, `add_resource_base_extension()`, and `register_native_struct()` perform writes without locking; however, they only operate during registration and cannot be called via the GDExtension interface.\nThere are also `cleanup_defaults()` and `cleanup()` during shutdown.\n\nThere is also a problem that adding a lock doesn't solve: `get_method()`, `get_method_with_compatibility()`, and `get_gdtype()` return pointers referencing ClassDB's internal data and release the lock upon returning. The caller holds that pointer without a lock, so if another thread removes the class, the pointer ends up pointing to invalid memory.\nI considered two solutions, but both require changing the API: returning a copy or forcing the caller to hold the lock. There are 27 instances in total (20 for `get_method`, 5 for `get_method_with_compatibility`, and 2 for `get_gdtype`). The volume isn't the issue, but the approach is; I don't know which path should be taken. Also, these are just the issues I found—I've looked quite thoroughly, but I can't guarantee these will make ClassDB *fully* thread-safe. If you show me the way, I can continue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5724750544/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]